[ ] Project workspaces to the V5 graph in Core =v5-projection $The core code change of Decision 43. Replace the v4 projection in clearhead-core rdf/project.rs and rdf/mod.rs with the mapping the spec defines, emitting no v4 terms. Prove it against the spec's fixture and shapes at Core's spec-conformance boundary, as the JSON schema conformance already runs, and check reasoner consistency with the ontology. Expect the graph to grow about tenfold per action; measure load and query time on this workspace before and after. ADDED 2026-10-01: the spec now requires times as written (no offset unless the file wrote one; date-only as xsd:date). Core's domain stores DateTime<Local>, so today's projection stamps the machine's offset and differs between time zones; the projection, or the domain, must keep what was written.$ !1 ^2026-10-01T20:22 <01a0faa2-17ea-778f-a8ae-a59285498e28 <019f5895-6948-70b2-88e2-a7685b0dddda #01a0faa2-7184-74d1-ae6c-1959f4af7fe3
[ ] Move the saved queries to the V5 graph with unchanged rows =v5-queries $Rewrite every saved query in clearhead-cli src/queries and the CLI's sparql modules against the new graph, plus this workspace's .clearhead/queries/for-human.sparql. Row shapes stay as they are, so nvim and other clients do not change; the existing query tests are the net, so freeze their expected rows before rewriting. The competency queries in ontology v5/queries are the working templates. ADDED 2026-10-01: the graph will carry no storage facts (spec convention 3, the human's call: no file paths, lines, roots or calendar ids, since another backend such as sqlite would have none). Today's rows include source_file and source_line, used by nvim to jump to source, and some index queries join through the ws:Workspace node. Keep the rows unchanged by having the implementation add locations after the query, joining each row's IRI against the loaded workspace; remove every ws: pattern from the queries. REVISED 2026-10-01 with the human: rows lose source_file, source_line and charter_root instead of the CLI adding them back; clients get locations from the new locate command. The row shapes therefore do change for those columns, and nvim moves with them (nvim-locate).$ !2 ^2026-10-01T20:22 <01a0fb02-e644-7317-88ad-1e76ecfb2b0e #01a0faa2-71a3-70a1-91c5-a485dedd4de2
[ ] Retire the v4 vocabulary everywhere =retire-v4 $Remove the v4 namespace constants and fixtures from clearhead-core, the ontology's v4 directory, examples and queries, its pytest suite and pyproject deps, and V4_DESIGN.md; point specifications/ontology.md readers at the ontology's docs/domain.md. Decide then whether clearhead.us keeps serving the v4 vocabulary for anyone holding its IRIs (cool URIs do not change) or drops it with the site.$ !3 ^2026-10-01T20:22 <01a0faa2-71a3-70a1-91c5-a485dedd4de2 #01a0faa2-71c0-7365-9b59-8baa79bf9766
[ ] Resolve locations in nvim through clearhead locate =nvim-locate $Per Decision 44, query rows will carry identities, not locations. view.lua (quickfix: charter_root, source_file, source_line) and tree_view.lua (source_file, source_line) must take the row ids, call clearhead locate once for the whole list, and build entries from its answer. Land together with v5-queries so the plugin never sees rows without a way to locate them.$ !2 ^2026-10-01T22:07 <01a0fb02-e644-7317-88ad-1e76ecfb2b0e #01a0fb02-e66c-74e2-bb7d-bd6b4fb04e2a
[ ] Extend the graph fixture to recurring plans and objective states =v5-fixture-gaps $The graph fixture in specifications/examples/conformance/graph covers every action field and state, charters, objectives, contexts and waits, but not: an .ics recurring plan with a materialized occurrence (when/recurrence, RRULE text, occurrence as part of the recurring action), and an objective state, whose vocabulary objectives.md does not define yet (Decision 5 says objectives have state, confirmed by an agent). Settle the objective state values with the objectives-into-Core work, then add both to the workspace, expected.ttl and the shapes, with an invalid graph for each new rule.$ !3 ^2026-10-01T22:27 #01a0fb14-c5e6-73d8-9c0d-f56f11ce00a6
[ ] Show the actions that serve an objective =objective-actions-view $Moved out of the objectives action, 2026-10-01: answering it is a query (an objective's plans, then everything they contain), which V5 makes a has-continuant-part walk from the plans that name the objective. Write it as a saved query once v5-queries has moved the queries to the new graph, then surface it in the CLI and nvim like the other named queries.$ !3 ^2026-10-01T22:35 <01a0faa2-71a3-70a1-91c5-a485dedd4de2 #01a0fb1c-4455-7218-bc00-d4d38247de78
